			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Expand parameter extraction utilities for IPC dispatch\n\nExtend the `Utilities::Params` module with typed helpers (`i64_at`, `u64_at_or`, `obj_str`, `obj_val`, etc.) to handle both positional arrays and JSON object payloads without inline boilerplate. Introduce `obj_*` variants specifically for named-key extraction used by UI service providers.\n\nApply these new utilities across the `CreateEffectForRequest` tree (Debug, LanguageFeatures, SCM, Secrets, StatusBar, Terminal, TreeView, UserInterface, Webview) to replace verbose `get().and_then().unwrap_or()` chains. This unifies parameter parsing logic, reduces code duplication, and ensures consistent default handling for handles, strings, numbers, and boolean flags across all IPC request handlers.",
			"SHA": "c3502e8e72ddeeae430be9c7966678f2a26dc22f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T15:42:48Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				2
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Cocoon and Mountain submodules for build refresh and IPC standardization\n\nUpdate the Cocoon and Mountain element submodules to align with recent refactorings in the native backend IPC layer and extension host build pipeline.\n\n**Cocoon:** Regenerate all ESBuild output artifacts in `Target/` and update `Source/Generated/RouteManifest.ts` with the current compilation timestamp. This ensures the extension host bootstrap and RPC method handlers are synchronized with the latest source state following upstream service layer changes.\n\n**Mountain:** Refactor `WindowUI` and `Workspace` IPC handlers to utilize new centralized utility functions (`array_unwrap`, `uri_from_params`, `ensure_array`) from the `Utilities::Params` module. Replace inline conditional logic for unwrapping JSON arrays and normalizing URI parameters, eliminating duplicated type checks and ensuring consistent argument normalization across Tauri event handlers.\n\n**Impact:** These changes maintain binary artifact consistency for the extension host and further reduce boilerplate in the native backend dispatch layer, reinforcing the project's Effect-based architectural principles.",
			"SHA": "b20c14839d0ecbd28de8cff661e8e3e99ec8e054"
		}
